## Historical background
### Physical characteristics
The structural load is supported by a stressed-skin design.[[77]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateway_Arch#cite_note-Freeman-83) Each leg is embedded in 25,980 short tons (23,570 t) of concrete 44 feet (13 m) thick[[66]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateway_Arch#cite_note-Bryant-71) and 60 feet (18 m) deep.[[78]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateway_Arch#cite_note-Sutton-84)Twenty feet (6.1 m) of the foundation is in bedrock.[[78]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateway_Arch#cite_note-Sutton-84) The arch is resistant to earthquakes[[79]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateway_Arch#cite_note-National_Parks_1998-85) and is designed to sway up to 18 inches (46 cm) in either direction,[[80]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateway_Arch#cite_note-86) while withstanding winds up to 150 miles per hour (240 km/h).[[81]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateway_Arch#cite_note-Post-Dispatch-87) The structure weighs 42,878 short tons (38,898 t), of which concrete composes 25,980 short tons (23,570 t); structural steel interior, 2,157 short tons (1,957 t);

